# Analects Book 9 (子罕) — draft, second half: lemmata 22–44 = passages 9.12–9.30.
# Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary.
# Passage numbering follows Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (凡三十章; the ○ marks agree with 9.12–9.30): 9.13 runs
# over two units, 9.26 over three, 9.30 over two. He Yan's text runs 唐棣之華… (9.30) straight on from the
# 權 saying (9.29) and his commentary reads the Ode as illustrating 權; Zhu Xi names that joining as the
# error behind the 反經合道 theory and prints them as two chapters. He Yan's heading counts 31 chapters
# (Huang Kan 30); the archived He Yan text marks no breaks, so where his extra division falls is not shown.
# Quotation marks balance within every unit; a saying that runs on past one of Zhu Xi's interruptions
# (9.26: the Ode line 不忮不求… in lemma 38) is left unquoted in the continuing unit, as 8.13. The Ode of
# 9.30 (lemma 43) stands without a speaker and is left unquoted (a unit cannot open with punctuation).
# Glyphs kept as the edition prints them: 徳 (= 德), 徃 (= 往), 囘 (= 回), 栢 (= 柏), 顔 (= 顏), 説 and 說
# (both in lemma 34), 已 (read yǐ in 也已 / 也已矣).
# Lemma 35 (9.24) repeats the second half of 1.8 (Zhu Xi: 重出而逸其半); its l and i are those shipped for 1.8.
# Readings Zhu Xi marks that modern practice does not keep: 韞 and 縕 (紆粉反, yǔn; we give yùn).
# Kept: 賈 jià (音嫁, 'price'), 舍 shě (上聲), 夫 fú (音扶, 9.16, 9.21, 9.30), 好 hào (去聲, 9.17),
# 簣 kuì (求位反), 覆 fù (芳服反), 語 yù (去聲, 9.19), 與 yú (平聲, 9.19, 9.26), 焉 yān (於虔反, 9.22),
# 衣 yì (去聲, 9.26), 貉 hé (胡各反), 忮 zhì (之豉反), 棣 dì (大計反).
# New bound compounds (need glossary entries): 匹夫 pǐ fū, 後生 hòu shēng, 唐棣 táng dì.
# Existing bound compounds used: 子貢, 君子, 如之何, 顔淵, 子路, 三軍.

